    20                                  ; Section(s): CPSC 240-#8, CPSC 240-#7
    21                                  ; Email: akhajuria@csu.fullerton.edu
    22                                  ;
    23                                  ; Program Information:
    24                                  ; Name: Assignment 4 - Taylor Series
    25                                  ; Languages: C++, x86-64 Assembly, Bash
    26                                  ; Completion Date: 11/06/2026
    27                                  ;
    28                                  ; Program's Purpose:
    29                                  ; This program approximates e^x using a Taylor series consisting of
    30                                  ; n+1 terms. It accepts a floating-point value x and an integer n
    31                                  ; from the user, computes the approximation, and displays the result
    32                                  ; with eight digits after the decimal point.
    33                                  ;
    34                                  ; Project Information:
    35                                  ; Files: main.cpp, series.asm, taylor.asm, macro.inc, r.sh
    36                                  ; Status: Complete
    37                                  ;
    38                                  ; Execution:
    39                                  ; Run ./r.sh.
    40                                  ; The script assembles, compiles, links, and executes the program.
    41                                  ;
    42                                  ; File's Purpose:
    43                                  ; This file contains the series function, which obtains the user's
    44                                  ; input values x and n, passes them to the taylor function, receives
    45                                  ; the computed approximation, displays it, and returns the result
    46                                  ; to the C++ driver.
    47                                  
